            <ArticleTitle>Silent ischemic cardiomyopathy and left coronary ostial stenosis secondary to radiation therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>260-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 55-year-old woman presented with profound congestive heart failure 23 years following mediastinal radiation. Ejection fraction (EF) was 35%. Symptoms markedly improved and EF increased to &gt; 55% following saphenous vein bypass for &gt; or = 80% ostial left main stenosis. Radiation therapy, a known risk factor for coronary atherosclerosis, may present with reversible severe silent ischemia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
